{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":209515,"duration_api_ms":208276,"num_turns":24,"result":"Perfect! I've successfully generated the workflow knowledge report. Here is the complete file content:\n\n---\n\n# 1000 Genomes Workflow Knowledge Report\n\n**Workflow Name:** 1000genome\n**Analysis Agent:** Claude\n**Analysis Date:** 2026-03-11\n**Scope:** Static code analysis only (DAG structure, task logic, data flows)\n\n---\n\n## Executive Summary\n\nThe 1000 Genomes workflow is a bioinformatics pipeline for analyzing human genetic variation. It processes whole-chromosome variant data (VCF files), annotates variants with functional impact scores (SIFT), and computes mutation overlap statistics within and across populations. The workflow exhibits **per-chromosome and per-population parallelism** with a multi-stage DAG structure orchestrated by Pegasus WMS.\n\n---\n\n## Step 1: Repository Structure\n\n### Directory and File Layout\n\n```\n1000genome-workflow/\n├── daxgen.py              # Pegasus DAX generator (task spawn logic)\n├── data.csv               # Chromosome inventory (vcf, lines, annotation_vcf)\n├── prepare_input.sh       # Input preparation script\n├── env.sh                 # Environment configuration\n├── README.md              # Project documentation\n├── bin/                   # Task executables\n│   ├── individuals.py     # VCF parser\n│   ├── individuals_merge.py\n│   ├── sifting.py         # SIFT annotation filter\n│   ├── mutation_overlap.py\n│   └── frequency.py\n├── data/\n│   ├── 20130502/          # Dataset version directory\n│   │   ├── ALL.chr1.250000.vcf, ...   # Per-chromosome VCF files\n│   │   ├── columns.txt               # Individual ID metadata\n│   │   └── sifting/                  # VEP annotation files\n│   └── populations/       # Population membership lists\n│       ├── AFR, ALL, AMR, EAS, EUR, GBR, SAS\n└── analysis/              # Post-execution analysis scripts (not part of workflow)\n```\n\n### Workflow Entry Point\n\n`daxgen.py` is the primary generator. It:\n1. Reads `data.csv` to enumerate chromosomes\n2. Reads `data/populations/` to identify available populations\n3. Instantiates tasks based on parameters (`ind_jobs`, `exec_site`, etc.)\n4. Writes Pegasus DAX workflow file (default name: `1000-genome-{timestamp}.yml`)\n\n---\n\n## Step 2: Identify Stages and Tasks\n\n### Five Task Types (Five Logical Stages)\n\n#### **Task 1: Individuals**\n- **Executable:** `bin/individuals.py`\n- **Inputs:**\n  - `ALL.chrX.250000.vcf` (one per chromosome; ~250,000 lines)\n  - `columns.txt` (individual ID list)\n  - Parameters: chromosome number, start line, stop line, total lines\n- **Outputs:**\n  - `chrXn-{start}-{stop}.tar.gz` (compressed archive of per-individual mutation files)\n- **Processing:**\n  - Reads VCF file in line range [start, stop)\n  - Filters lines: removes VCF headers (lines starting with `#`)\n  - For each individual (column), extracts SNPs with specific allele frequency (AF) thresholds\n  - Writes one file per individual: `chrX.{individual_id}`\n  - Compresses archive for staging efficiency\n- **Parallelism:** Multiple jobs per chromosome (parameterized by `ind_jobs`; default 1, max 250)\n- **Cardinality per chromosome:** `ind_jobs` (1 to 250)\n\n#### **Task 2: Individuals_Merge**\n- **Executable:** `bin/individuals_merge.py`\n- **Inputs:**\n  - All `chrXn-{start}-{stop}.tar.gz` files from Individuals tasks for chromosome X\n  - Parameter: chromosome number\n- **Outputs:**\n  - `chrXn.tar.gz` (merged archive with all individuals for the chromosome)\n- **Processing:**\n  - Extracts input tar files to temporary directory\n  - Merges per-individual files (concatenates content by filename)\n  - Re-compresses into single tarball\n- **Parallelism:** One job per chromosome\n- **Cardinality:** `num_chromosomes`\n\n#### **Task 3: Sifting**\n- **Executable:** `bin/sifting.py`\n- **Inputs:**\n  - `ALL.chrX.phase3_shapeit2_mvncall_integrated_v5.20130502.sites.annotation.vcf` (VEP-annotated VCF)\n  - Parameter: chromosome number\n- **Outputs:**\n  - `sifted.SIFT.chrX.txt` (space-separated: line_number, rs_id, ENSG_id, SIFT_score, phenotype)\n- **Processing:**\n  - Scans VEP annotation VCF for lines containing \"deleterious\" or \"tolerated\"\n  - Filters to lines with rs-number variant IDs\n  - Parses pipe-delimited (|) VEP INFO field (column 8) to extract SIFT, ENSG, phenotype\n  - Adjusts line numbers relative to header count\n  - Writes filtered, reformatted output\n- **Parallelism:** One job per chromosome\n- **Cardinality:** `num_chromosomes`\n\n#### **Task 4: Mutation_Overlap**\n- **Executable:** `bin/mutation_overlap.py`\n- **Inputs:**\n  - `chrXn.tar.gz` (merged individual mutation files)\n  - `sifted.SIFT.chrX.txt` (SIFT annotations)\n  - Population file (e.g., `EUR`, containing newline-separated individual IDs)\n  - `columns.txt` (individual ID metadata)\n  - Parameters: `-c {chromosome}`, `-pop {population}`\n- **Outputs:**\n  - Multiple text files (overlap matrices, gene pair counts, individual mutation counts)\n  - PNG plots (histograms, colormaps)\n  - All packed into `chrX-{population}.tar.gz` (staged out)\n- **Processing:**\n  - Extracts individuals archive\n  - Reads population list and filters to matching individual IDs\n  - Loads per-individual mutation files (rs numbers)\n  - Computes all-pairs pairwise intersections of mutation sets\n  - Generates symmetric and half-pair overlap matrices\n  - Counts gene pair co-occurrences\n  - Produces visualization plots using matplotlib\n- **Parallelism:** One job per chromosome × population combination\n- **Cardinality:** `num_chromosomes × num_populations` (e.g., 10 × 7 = 70 with default data)\n\n#### **Task 5: Frequency**\n- **Executable:** `bin/frequency.py`\n- **Inputs:** Same as Mutation_Overlap (same parameters)\n- **Outputs:**\n  - Multiple text files per iteration (histogram, raw overlap counts, random individual IDs, mutation lists)\n  - PNG plot histograms (one per run)\n  - All packed into `chrX-{population}-freq.tar.gz` (staged out)\n- **Processing:**\n  - Extracts individuals archive\n  - Loads per-individual mutations\n  - **Runs 1000 Monte Carlo iterations internally:**\n    - Each iteration: randomly select 52 individuals\n    - Count overlapping mutations (multiset intersection)\n    - Record frequency histogram\n  - Produces plots for each run\n- **Parallelism:** One job per chromosome × population combination\n- **Cardinality:** `num_chromosomes × num_populations`\n\n---\n\n## Step 3: Data Object Registry\n\n### Input Data Objects (External)\n\n| Name | Format | Size Estimate | Purpose |\n|------|--------|---------------|---------|\n| `ALL.chrX.250000.vcf` | VCF text | ~1-2 GB per file | Chromosome genotypes (Phase3, ~2504 individuals) |\n| `ALL.chrX.*.annotation.vcf` | VEP-annotated VCF | ~500 MB per file | Variant effect predictions (SIFT scores) |\n| `columns.txt` | Tab-separated text | ~50 KB | Individual ID list (sample metadata) |\n| Population lists (AFR, ALL, AMR, EAS, EUR, GBR, SAS) | Newline-separated text | ~1-5 KB each | Individual IDs per population |\n\n### Intermediate Data Objects (Workflow-Generated)\n\n| Name | Format | Producer | Consumer | Purpose |\n|------|--------|----------|----------|---------|\n| `chrXn-{start}-{stop}.tar.gz` | gzip tar archive | Individuals | Individuals_Merge | Per-chunk per-individual files |\n| `chrXn.tar.gz` | gzip tar archive | Individuals_Merge | Mutation_Overlap, Frequency | Complete per-individual mutations (not staged out) |\n| `sifted.SIFT.chrX.txt` | Space-separated text | Sifting | Mutation_Overlap, Frequency | SIFT annotation lookup (not staged out) |\n\n### Output Data Objects (Staged Out)\n\n| Name | Format | Producer | Purpose |\n|------|--------|----------|---------|\n| `chrX-{population}.tar.gz` | gzip tar archive | Mutation_Overlap | Overlap statistics + plots per chromosome × population |\n| `chrX-{population}-freq.tar.gz` | gzip tar archive | Frequency | Frequency distributions (1000 runs) + plots |\n\n### Data Object Relationships\n\n```\nInputs:\n  VCF → Individuals → chrXn-{start}-{stop}.tar.gz → Individuals_Merge → chrXn.tar.gz ⇝ Outputs\n  VEP Annotation → Sifting → sifted.SIFT.chrX.txt ────────────────────────────────┐\n  columns.txt ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n  Population files ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n                                                                                     ⇝ Mutation_Overlap ⇝ chrX-{pop}.tar.gz\n                                                                                     ├ Frequency ⇝ chrX-{pop}-freq.tar.gz\n```\n\n---\n\n## Step 4: Producer-Consumer Edge Map\n\n### Task Dependencies (Expressed as Edges)\n\n| Source → Sink | Type | Rationale |\n|---------------|------|-----------|\n| Individuals → Individuals_Merge | **Data** | Multiple task outputs aggregated into one |\n| Individuals_Merge → Mutation_Overlap | **Data** | Analysis depends on merged individuals file |\n| Individuals_Merge → Frequency | **Data** | Analysis depends on merged individuals file |\n| Sifting → Mutation_Overlap | **Data** | SIFT scores required for variant filtering |\n| Sifting → Frequency | **Data** | SIFT scores required for variant filtering |\n| columns.txt → Individuals | **Metadata** | Individual ID mapping |\n| columns.txt → Mutation_Overlap | **Metadata** | Individual ID mapping |\n| columns.txt → Frequency | **Metadata** | Individual ID mapping |\n| Population file → Mutation_Overlap | **Metadata** | Population membership filter |\n| Population file → Frequency | **Metadata** | Population membership filter |\n\n### Dependency Patterns by Chromosome\n\nFor each chromosome X:\n- **Phase 1 (Independent):** Individuals and Sifting tasks execute with no mutual dependencies\n- **Phase 2 (Merge):** Individuals_Merge waits for all Individuals tasks to complete\n- **Phase 3 (Analysis):** Mutation_Overlap and Frequency tasks start after Individuals_Merge AND Sifting complete\n\n### Cross-Chromosome Dependencies\n\n**None.** Each chromosome is processed completely independently; no data flow between chromosomes.\n\n### Cross-Population Dependencies\n\n**None.** Each population is analyzed independently; no data flow between populations.\n\n---\n\n## Step 5: Workflow-Level Pattern Analysis\n\n### DAG Topology Classification\n\n**Type:** Directed Acyclic Graph (DAG) with **multi-dimensional parallelism**\n\n**Dimensions:**\n1. **Per-Chromosome (Primary):** All chromosomes (10 visible in data.csv) are independent and fully parallelizable\n2. **Intra-Chromosome (Optional):** Individuals task can split into 1-250 parallel jobs per chromosome\n3. **Per-Population (Secondary):** After per-chromosome merge, 7 independent population analyses fan out\n\n### Execution Pattern (Control Flow)\n\n```\nFOR EACH chromosome IN data.csv:\n  SPAWN Individuals task(s):     1 to ind_jobs parallel jobs\n  SPAWN Sifting task:             1 job\n  SYNCHRONIZE (barrier):          Wait for Individuals_Merge\n    SPAWN Individuals_Merge:       1 job\n    WAIT FOR Individuals_Merge and Sifting\n\n    FOR EACH population IN populations/:\n      SPAWN Mutation_Overlap:      1 job\n      SPAWN Frequency:             1 job\n      (can run in parallel with other populations)\n```\n\n### Cardinality Summary\n\n| Task Type | Count | Formula |\n|-----------|-------|---------|\n| Individuals | **10–2500** | `num_chromosomes × [1, ind_jobs]` |\n| Individuals_Merge | **10** | `num_chromosomes` |\n| Sifting | **10** | `num_chromosomes` |\n| Mutation_Overlap | **70** | `num_chromosomes × num_populations` (10 × 7) |\n| Frequency | **70** | `num_chromosomes × num_populations` (10 × 7) |\n| **Total (without parallelism)** | **230** | Base case: ind_jobs=1 |\n| **Total (with max parallelism)** | **2660** | Max case: ind_jobs=250 |\n\n### Synchronization Points (Merge Barriers)\n\n1. **Per-Chromosome Merge Barrier:** Individuals_Merge task must wait for all Individuals tasks of the same chromosome\n2. **Pre-Analysis Barrier:** Both Mutation_Overlap and Frequency must wait for Individuals_Merge + Sifting completion\n\n### Branching and Iteration\n\n- **Branching:** No conditional branching (all tasks are deterministic)\n- **Iteration:** Frequency task runs 1000 internal Monte Carlo iterations per job (not workflow-level parallelism)\n- **Parallelism Model:** Task-level data parallelism; no loops in DAG definition\n\n---\n\n## Step 6: I/O Behavioral Hints (Static Analysis Only)\n\n### Large-File Streaming Patterns\n\n1. **Individuals Task:**\n   - **I/O Pattern:** Stream read of VCF (~1-2 GB); line-by-line filtering\n   - **Evidence:** Code reads file content, processes in line range `[counter, stop)`, filters\n   - **Hint:** Sequential scan without random access; suitable for streaming\n\n2. **Sifting Task:**\n   - **I/O Pattern:** Grep-based filter on VEP annotation VCF; shell subprocess invocation\n   - **Evidence:** `subprocess.run([\"grep ...\"], ...)` at line 45 in sifting.py\n   - **Hint:** External command execution; may have performance overhead vs. native Python filtering\n\n### Intermediate File Proliferation\n\n- **Individuals output:** Creates one file per individual per job (~2500 files per chunk)\n- **Packaging strategy:** Tar.gz compression used to reduce staging overhead\n- **Hint:** Small-file overhead likely; tarball wrapping is mitigation strategy\n\n### Data Reuse Without Caching\n\n1. **Sifted file:** Read by both Mutation_Overlap and Frequency; no caching observed\n   - **Size:** ~1-5 KB (small; recomputation cost negligible)\n2. **Individuals archive:** Extracted fresh by each analysis task (Mutation_Overlap and Frequency)\n   - **Pattern:** Redundant extraction if tasks co-locate; could benefit from shared filesystem\n3. **Population files:** Copied to each task working directory; no memoization\n\n### Format Transformations\n\n1. **VCF → Per-Individual Text:**\n   - **Input:** Column-oriented VCF (variants × individuals)\n   - **Output:** Row-oriented text files (one per individual)\n   - **Hint:** Format change requires full data scan and writes\n2. **VEP Pipe-Delimited Field Parsing:**\n   - **Pattern:** String splits on pipes (|); index extraction of specific fields\n   - **Hint:** Complex parsing; vulnerable to field order assumptions\n\n### Metadata-Heavy Patterns\n\n1. **Individual ID Mapping:**\n   - **Sources:** VCF column headers, population files, columns.txt\n   - **Operation:** Three-way set intersection (code at lines 85 in mutation_overlap.py)\n   - **Hint:** O(N) operations; could optimize with hash maps\n2. **VCF Header Scanning:**\n   - **Pattern:** Scans first ~1000 lines to count headers (regex at line 27 in sifting.py)\n   - **Hint:** Linear scan; could be cached if processed multiple times\n\n### Potential I/O Bottlenecks (Inferred from Code)\n\n1. **Repeated Tar Extraction:**\n   - `chrXn.tar.gz` extracted by both Mutation_Overlap and Frequency for same chromosome\n   - **[ASSUMPTION]** No inter-task data sharing; redundant extraction cost unknown\n2. **Pairwise Set Intersections (in-memory):**\n   - Mutation_Overlap computes N² pairs for N individuals (~2500)\n   - **[ASSUMPTION]** Full matrix allocated upfront; sparse or triangular representation not visible\n3. **PNG Plot Generation:**\n   - No explicit guidance on plot file sizes; matplotlib memory/time cost unknown\n\n---\n\n## Step 7: Assemble and Validate Report\n\n### Cross-Reference Validation\n\n✓ All tasks defined in `daxgen.py` (lines 179–214) match executable files in `bin/`\n✓ All populations in `data/populations/` (7 files) match hardcoded list in README\n✓ All task inputs/outputs trace correctly through daxgen.py job definitions (lines 400–469)\n✓ No circular dependencies; DAG structure verified\n\n### Consistency Checks\n\n| Item | Source | Status |\n|------|--------|--------|\n| Task count | daxgen.py | 5 tasks (individuals, individuals_merge, sifting, mutation_overlap, frequency) |\n| Chromosome count | data.csv | 10 chromosomes visible (chr1–chr10); full dataset unknown |\n| Population count | data/populations/ | 7 populations (AFR, ALL, AMR, EAS, EUR, GBR, SAS) |\n| Individuals per chunk | individuals.py:56–62 | ~2500 (inferred from VCF column count; exact count not in code) |\n| Frequency iterations | frequency.py:38 | 1000 runs (hardcoded; not parameterized) |\n\n### Known Unknowns\n\n| Item | Status | Reason |\n|------|--------|--------|\n| Total chromosomes in full dataset | unknown | Only 10 visible in data.csv (example data) |\n| Exact SIFT filtering threshold | unknown | Hardcoded as `'NO-SIFT'`; numeric threshold not visible |\n| Random seed for Monte Carlo | unknown | No seed set in frequency.py; results may vary |\n| Output archive structure | unknown | Code creates archives; internal subdirectory layout not specified in code |\n| Memory constraints | unknown | No hard limits in daxgen.py; README provides empirical observations only |\n\n---\n\n## Summary\n\n### Workflow Overview\n\n| Aspect | Value |\n|--------|-------|\n| **Primary Parallelism** | Per-chromosome (embarrassingly parallel) |\n| **Secondary Parallelism** | Per-population analysis (7-way fan-out) |\n| **Optional Parallelism** | Intra-chromosome Individuals splits (1–250) |\n| **DAG Type** | Multi-stage aggregation + fan-out |\n| **Task Count (min)** | 230 jobs (10 chr, ind_jobs=1) |\n| **Task Count (max)** | 2660 jobs (10 chr, ind_jobs=250) |\n| **Synchronization Points** | Per-chromosome merge barrier |\n| **Branching/Loops** | None (deterministic DAG) |\n\n### Data Flow Summary\n\n- **Input→Prepare:** VCF/Annotation → Individuals/Sifting (independent parallel)\n- **Prepare→Aggregate:** Individuals → Individuals_Merge (mandatory convergence)\n- **Aggregate→Analyze:** Merged individuals + SIFT → Mutation_Overlap + Frequency (population-parallel)\n- **Output:** Two result archives per chromosome-population pair\n\n### Static Code Insights\n\n1. **Staging Strategy:** Tarball compression of intermediate files (small-file mitigation)\n2. **Filtering Strategy:** Multi-stage filtering (AF-based in Individuals; SIFT-based in Sifting; population-based in analysis)\n3. **Analysis Model:** Stateless per-task analysis (no inter-task caching; ideal for distributed execution)\n4. **Metadata Dependence:** Heavy use of ID mapping (columns.txt, population files) for individual selection\n\n---\n\n*Report generated via static code analysis of daxgen.py, bin/*.py, data/, and configuration files. No runtime observations, performance profiling, or deployment details included.*\n\n---\n\nSTATUS: success | OUTPUT: /home/mtang11/scripts/workflow-representation-description/workflow_knowledge/1000genome-knowledge-claude-trial3.md","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"21efaf45-d743-457b-bf29-2890a2b0a733","total_cost_usd":0.28574155000000007,"usage":{"input_tokens":122,"cache_creation_input_tokens":72055,"cache_read_input_tokens":929958,"output_tokens":20511,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":72055,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":122,"outputTokens":20511,"cacheReadInputTokens":929958,"cacheCreationInputTokens":72055,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.28574155000000007,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"8f8f48e6-8258-43b0-8838-3ae77e9c52a9"}
